# =============================================================================
# kmousetool - Configuration Template
# =============================================================================
#
# PACKAGE OVERVIEW:
# kmousetool is a KDE utility that aids users with motor impairments or
# physical disabilities by automatically clicking the mouse pointer when it
# is held stationary over a window for a configurable amount of time.
#
# This package is a pure GUI application. It does NOT run as a background
# service, nor does it listen on network ports. It does not require a
# database, cache, or message queue. Configuration is typically handled
# via KDE System Settings or by editing the configuration file directly
# within the user's KDE configuration directory (e.g., ~/.config/kdeglobals
# or a dedicated kmousetoolrc).
#
# Because this is a client-side desktop application with no server daemon,
# there are no global service configuration directives to render here.
# The Ansible role managing this package should focus on:
#   1. Ensuring the package is installed.
#   2. Optionally applying desktop environment settings (e.g., via
#      kde-config or direct file manipulation in the user's home dir).
#
# NO CONFIGURATION DIRECTIVES AVAILABLE IN THIS TEMPLATE.
# =============================================================================